nce on iPhones: Up to 80 Tokens/Second on Apple Silicon\", {\n    x: 0.6, y: 0.1, w: 8.8, h: 0.7, fontSize: 19, fontFace: FONT_H, color: C.white, bold: true, margin: 0\n  });\n\n  // Left: Throughput stats\n  s8.addShape(pres.shapes.RECTANGLE, { x: 0.5, y: 1.15, w: 4.3, h: 3.8, fill: { color: C.white }, shadow: cardShadow() });\n  s8.addShape(pres.shapes.RECTANGLE, { x: 0.5, y: 1.15, w: 0.06, h: 3.8, fill: { color: C.teal } });\n\n  s8.addImage({ data: iconMobile, x: 0.8, y: 1.3, w: 0.35, h: 0.35 });\n  s8.addText(\"HuggingSnap iOS App\", {\n    x: 1.25, y: 1.3, w: 3.3, h: 0.35, fontSize: 14, fontFace: FONT_H, color: C.textDark, bold: true, margin: 0\n  });\n\n  s8.addText(\"Entirely local inference — no cloud dependency\", {\n    x: 0.8, y: 1.7, w: 3.8, h: 0.3, fontSize: 11, fontFace: FONT_B, color: C.textMuted, italic: true, margin: 0\n  });\n\n  // Throughput callouts\n  const tpStats = [\n    { device: \"MacBook Pro M1 Max 64GB\", speed: \"~80 tok/s\", note: \"batch=1, 256M model\", color: C.emerald },\n    { device: \"MacBook Air M3 16GB\", speed: \"~55 tok/s\", note: \"batch=1, 256M model\", color: C.teal },\n    { device: \"M1 Max 64GB (batch=64)\", speed: \"~1000 tok/s\", note: \"256M model, high throughput\", color: C.amber },\n  ];\n\n  let tpY = 2.15;\n  for (const tp of tpStats) {\n    s8.addText(tp.speed, { x: 0.8, y: tpY, w: 1.8, h: 0.4, fontSize: 20, fontFace: FONT_H, color: tp.color, bold: true, margin: 0 });\n    s8.addText(tp.device, { x: 2.6, y: tpY, w: 2.0, h: 0.22, fontSize: 10, fontFace: FONT_B, color: C.textDark, bold: true, margin: 0 });\n    s8.addText(tp.note, { x: 2.6, y: tpY + 0.2, w: 2.0, h: 0.2, fontSize: 9, fontFace: FONT_B, color: C.textMuted, margin: 0 });\n    tpY += 0.6;\n  }\n\n  s8.addText([\n    { text: \"Throughput scales roughly linearly with batch size for the 256M model.\", options: { breakLine: true, fontSize: 10, color: C.textMuted, italic: true } },\n  ], { x: 0.8, y: 4.05, w: 3.8, h: 0.6, valign: \"top\", margin: 0 });\n\n  // Right: Figure 2\n  s8.addShape(pres.shapes.RECTANGLE, { x: 5.2, y: 1.15, w: 4.3, h: 4.2, fill: { color: C.white }, shadow: cardShadow() });\n  s8.addImage({ data: imgFig2, x: 5.35, y: 1.3, w: 4.0, h: 3.9, sizing: { type: \"contain\", w: 4.0, h: 3.9 } });\n\n  // ==================== SLIDE 9: Key Takeaways ====================\n  let s9 = pres.addSlide();\n  s9.background = { color: C.darkBg };\n\n  // Top accent\n  s9.addShape(pres.shapes.RECTANGLE, { x: 0, y: 0, w: 10, h: 0.06, fill: { color: C.teal } });\n\n  s9.addText(\"Key Takeaways\", {\n    x: 0.6, y: 0.3, w: 8.8, h: 0.7, fontSize: 32, fontFace: FONT_H, color: C.white, bold: true, margin: 0\n  });\n  s9.addText(\"Design Principles for Efficient Multimodal Models\", {\n    x: 0.6, y: 0.95, w: 8.8, h: 0.4, fontSize: 16, fontFace: FONT_B, color: C.teal, margin: 0\n  });\n\n  // 5 principle cards\n  const principles = [\n    { num: \"1\", title: \"Balance Encoder-LM Compute\", desc: \"Smaller vision encoders (93M) outperform larger ones (428M) when paired with compact LMs.\", icon: iconCogs, color: C.teal },\n    { num: \"2\", title: \"Extend Context Length\", desc: \"Scaling from 2K to 16K tokens via RoPE adjustment unlocks higher-resolution inputs.\", icon: iconExpand, color: C.emerald },\n    { num: \"3\", title: \"Aggressive Token Compression\", desc: \"Pixel shuffle at r=4 yields 16× reduction for small models, easing attention costs.\", icon: iconCompress, color: C.amber },\n    { num: \"4\", title: \"Sub-1GB Inference Is Achievable\", desc: \"SmolVLM-256M runs at 0.8 GB RAM, surpassing the 300× larger Idefics-80B.\", icon: iconRocket, color: C.teal },\n    { num: \"5\", title: \"Fully Open-Source Release\", desc: \"All weights, data, code, and mobile app (HuggingSnap) are open-sourced.\", icon: iconCheck, color: C.emerald },\n  ];\n\n  let py = 1.55;\n  for (const p of principles) {\n    s9.addShape(pres.shapes.RECTANGLE, { x: 0.5, y: py, w: 9.0, h: 0.7, fill: { color: C.darkBg2 }, shadow: cardShadow() });\n    // Accent bar\n    s9.addShape(pres.shapes.RECTANGLE, { x: 0.5, y: py, w: 0.06, h: 0.7, fill: { color: p.color } });\n    // Number circle\n    s9.addShape(pres.shapes.OVAL, { x: 0.75, y: py + 0.12, w: 0.45, h: 0.45, fill: { color: p.color } });\n    s9.addText(p.num, { x: 0.75, y: py + 0.12, w: 0.45, h: 0.45, fontSize: 16, fontFace: FONT_H, color: C.white, bold: true, align: \"center\", valign: \"middle\", margin: 0 });\n    // Title and desc\n    s9.addText(p.title, { x: 1.35, y: py + 0.05, w: 7.8, h: 0.3, fontSize: 13, fontFace: FONT_H, color: C.white, bold: true, margin: 0 });\n    s9.addText(p.desc, { x: 1.35, y: py + 0.35, w: 7.8, h: 0.3, fontSize: 11, fontFace: FONT_B, color: C.slate300, margin: 0 });\n    py += 0.78;\n  }\n\n  // Bottom line\n  s9.addText(\"Efficient architecture > raw scale  •  On-device multimodal AI is here\", {\n    x: 0.6, y: 5.3, w: 8.8, h: 0.3, fontSize: 12, fontFace: FONT_H, color: C.teal, align: \"center\", margin: 0\n  });\n\n  // --- Write file ---\n  await pres.writeFile({ fileName: \"/app/output/final_deck.pptx\" });\n  console.log(\"Presentation saved to /app/output/final_deck.pptx\");\n}\n\nmain().catch(err => { console.error(err); process.exit(1); });\n", "numLines": 670, "startLine": 1, "totalLines": 670}}

